  <note>
    <content>
      <p>RK27 is a retrospective fixed-protein sequence-cluster transport validation on Kudla154, not an independent untouched confirmation or a protein-OOD experiment. The 150 exact CDS groups encode one GFP and were partitioned into 37 complete-linkage sequence clusters at 90 percent identity. Labels had previously been used in RK22 development.</p>
      <p>The frozen protocol compared simple features of CAI, CDS GC and CDS GC3 with the same features plus measured 5-prime MFE. Ridge and HistGB were evaluated over 10 seeds and 5 folds, producing 300 real CPU model fits. Primary inference used 20,000 sequence-cluster bootstrap replicates and 20,000 whole-cluster simple-structure swap permutations with four-endpoint Holm correction.</p>
      <p>Ridge Spearman gain is 0.9550512157495602 with 95 percent interval 0.4938143325215412 to 1.1068328448152622 and Holm-adjusted p 0.000199990000499975. Ridge MSE improvement is 0.15748870496429904 with interval 0.07131333997658695 to 0.21268609940042837 and Holm-adjusted p 0.0012999350032498376. HistGB Spearman gain is 0.4125779353547091 with interval 0.20882791150236585 to 0.5203177505533748 and Holm-adjusted p 0.00044997750112494374. HistGB MSE improvement is 0.10590705984382583 with interval 0.0422788346378453 to 0.1405610628854256 and Holm-adjusted p 0.0012999350032498376. Every effect is positive in 10 of 10 seeds.</p>
      <p>Primary-seed absolute OOD Spearman and MSE are minus 0.3184132230240836 and 0.2571487833252607 for ridge simple, 0.6366379927254766 and 0.09966007836096168 for ridge structure, 0.30242388253871244 and 0.1986577547399576 for HistGB simple, and 0.7150018178934215 and 0.09275069489613177 for HistGB structure. MFE-only arms are descriptive references; the confirmatory contrast remains structure versus simple.</p>
      <p>Independent verification passed 47 of 47 after rebuilding clustering, all model fits, predictions and resampling arrays; closeout evidence binding passed 97 of 97. Production result SHA256 is b601db3b0a5bec6b228492846f0058a0d959439c0eeebada05b749daa366ed5e and independent report SHA256 is 1e657146110a553071b169578839cbd0c45e357d9d4ff32394f297848d2df5f4. Science commit is 8a62836bb73b34bcae529bae6a21f6e3eefc85d1 and closeout commit is 95257f290062d0f7d1ad2ab7bab21eef0b485437. This result does not measure velocity or decay, establish full spatial coupling, read functional untouched data, authorize generator training or complete RK-G1.</p>
    </content>
